They didn't hesitate to head out to Lake Seminole to join in the search. As the hours ticked by without any breakthroughs, anxieties heightened that something terrible had happened to Mike. At 9pm, the helicopter was finally cleared to fly. It was grounded by midnight, having found nothing of significance. This didn't deter the ground-based search party, nor did the stormy winter night that had arrived. They braved the cold and continued to track the swampy foggy terrain.
他们毫不犹豫地前往塞米诺尔湖加入搜寻。随着时间一分一秒过去，却没有任何进展，人们越来越担心迈克发生了可怕的事情。晚上9点，直升机终于获准起飞。但到午夜时分，由于一无所获，直升机被迫停飞。这并没有阻止地面搜救队，也没有阻止那个风雨交加的冬夜。他们冒着严寒，继续在沼泽和雾气弥漫的地形中搜寻。

