00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:52.000
attached to a pair of overalls. Favoured by fishermen and duck hunters, they allow the wearer to stand in waist-high water without getting wet. For all their benefits, waders are also known to carry some risks. If someone falls in the water while wearing waders, the weight of the water can pull them down, while the pressure of the water can cause the fabric to suction onto their skin. This can make it incredibly difficult to remove the waders, thus dragging the wearer further down.
连体裤永久连接而成。深受渔民和猎鸭者喜爱，它们允许穿着者站在齐腰深的水中而不被弄湿。尽管有种种好处，涉水裤也存在一些风险。如果有人穿着涉水裤掉进水里，水的重量会把他们往下拉，而水的压力会导致织物吸附在皮肤上。这会使脱掉涉水裤变得极其困难，从而将穿着者进一步拖入水中。

15
00:09:52.000 --> 00:10:35.000
Although the lake was only 8 feet deep at its deepest point, with Mike's waders quickly filling with water, officers believed he could have been dragged under the surface. His boat could have then continued on without him until it came to a stop once hitting the muddy bank. One official remarked, When we find the waders, we will find Mike. At first light on the morning of Sunday December 17, FWC officers entered the water in a boat that was specially designed to navigate the heavily vegetated waters of Stump Lake.
虽然湖泊最深处只有8英尺，但随着迈克的涉水裤迅速进水，官员们认为他可能被拖到了水面下。他的船可能在他离开后继续漂流，直到撞上泥泞的河岸才停下。一位官员评论道：“当我们找到涉水裤时，我们就会找到迈克。”12月17日星期日清晨，FWC官员乘坐一艘专门设计用于在树桩湖茂密植被水域中航行的船只进入水中。

